1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:08,790
Slide 17 diagrams our core engineering model: "ASYNCHRONOUS ENGINE: THE 3-LAYER SPARK PIPELINE."

2
00:00:09,490 --> 00:00:14,240
Notice the three vertical layers clearly mapped in our architecture diagram.

3
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:30,300
Layer 1 at the top is the "Trigger Layer." This layer listens for incoming events—Webhook triggers from GitHub, Cron schedules running every midnight, or File Watchers detecting newly uploaded documents in Google Drive.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:44,250
Layer 2 in the center is the "Reasoning Layer." Powered by Gemini Flash, this layer parses the event, selects the appropriate tool schema, executes iterative planning steps, and validates data formats.

5
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:59,280
Layer 3 at the bottom is the "Action Layer." This layer executes the real-world payload—writing clean spreadsheets to Google Drive, appending logs to a database, and dispatching summary alerts.

6
00:00:59,980 --> 00:01:07,420
By decoupling Triggers, Reasoning, and Actions, your system becomes infinitely scalable and resilient to failures.

